# Private Connect — Product Context

## What it is

A hub-and-spoke connectivity platform. Agents run on machines, expose local services, and reach remote services by name. All traffic is E2E encrypted (X25519 + AES-256-GCM). No VPN, no open ports.

## Monorepo structure

| Path | What | Stack |
|------|------|-------|
| `apps/api` | Hub API server | NestJS, Prisma, PostgreSQL, Socket.IO |
| `apps/web` | Dashboard SPA | Nuxt 3 (SPA mode), Vue 3, Tailwind v4 |
| `apps/agent` | CLI + daemon | Node.js, compiled to binary via `pkg` |
| `packages/cli` | `npx private-connect` commands | Node.js (no auth required) |
| `packages/sdk` | `@privateconnect/sdk` | TypeScript |
| `integrations/` | OpenClaw skill | Markdown + config |
| `docs/` | All documentation | Markdown |

## Key concepts

- **Workspace** — tenant boundary. All resources (agents, services, API keys, shares) belong to one workspace. Isolated by RLS + application-level scoping.
- **Agent** — a machine running the CLI (`connect up`). Authenticates with a 256-bit token (SHA-256 hashed at rest). Tokens expire after 30 days.
- **Service** — a `host:port` exposed by an agent (`connect expose`). Reached by name (`connect reach`).
- **Temporary tunnel** — `npx private-connect tunnel <port>`. No auth. 2h default, 24h max. Separate from authenticated tunnels.
- **Share** — `connect share` / `connect join <code>`. Shares all services from one agent to another.
- **Grant** — scoped, time-limited API access for AI agents (`connect grant`).
- **Debug session** — real-time traffic inspection with AI copilot (`connect expose --debug`).

## CLI commands (authenticated)

`connect up`, `connect expose`, `connect reach`, `connect share`, `connect join`, `connect clone`, `connect link`, `connect delete`, `connect proxy`, `connect daemon`, `connect dev`, `connect dns`, `connect mcp`, `connect shell`, `connect grant`, `connect status`, `connect doctor`, `connect whoami`, `connect update`, `connect logout`

## CLI commands (npx, no auth)

`npx private-connect tunnel <port>`, `npx private-connect up <ports...>`, `npx private-connect join <code>`, `npx private-connect test <target>`, `npx private-connect <provider> <port>`

## API rate limits (ThrottlerGuard, global)

| Tier | Limit |
|------|-------|
| Short | 10 req/sec |
| Medium | 100 req/min |
| Long | 1000 req/hour |

WebSocket gateways, `/health`, and `/v1/status` are `@SkipThrottle()`.

## Auth patterns

- User: passwordless magic links, HTTP-only session cookies
- Agent: 256-bit token via `connect up` or `POST /v1/agents/provision`
- API: `pc_` prefixed keys, `x-api-key` header
- Guards: `AuthGuard` (session), `ApiKeyGuard`, `CombinedAuthGuard` (either), `AdminGuard`

## Public endpoints (no auth)

`/health`, `/v1/status`, `/docs`, `/openapi.json`, `/v1/auth/*`, `/v1/device/*`, `/v1/tunnels/temporary/*`, `/v1/ask`, `/share/*`, `/t/*`, `/v1/debug/public/*`

## Environment variables (important)

| Var | Where | Purpose |
|-----|-------|---------|
| `DATABASE_URL` | API | PostgreSQL connection |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | API | Comma-separated WebSocket origin allowlist |
| `CONNECT_HUB_URL` | Agent/SDK | Hub URL (default: `https://api.privateconnect.co`) |
| `PRIVATECONNECT_API_KEY` | SDK/CI | API key for programmatic access |
| `MAX_TEMP_TUNNEL_TTL_MINUTES` | API | Max temporary tunnel TTL (default: 1440 = 24h) |

